{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OrangeThemeAccordionComponentTokensProvider","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"code":["    \/\/ Define your own provider for accordion component tokens","    \/\/ by inheriting from existing provider","    class CustomAccordionComponentTokensProvider: OrangeThemeAccordionComponentTokensProvider {","","        \/\/ Then override the accordion component tokens you want.","","        override var spacePaddingBlockBottomExpandContainerDefault: SpaceSemanticToken { DimensionRawTokens._100 }","","        \/\/ ...","    }","","    \/\/ Or define your own provider from scratch","    class CustomAccordionComponentTokensProvider: AllAccordionComponentTokens {","","        \/\/ And implement hundreds of tokens.","        \/\/ You are allowed to give semantic tokens providers if you want to define values.","    }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Then, you can give this ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomAccordionComponentTokensProvider"},{"text":" to your own theme implementation:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["class LocalTheme: OrangeTheme {","","    override init() {","        super.init(accordion: CustomAccordionComponentTokensProvider())","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"or to an already existing theme for example:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["    OrangeTheme(accordion: CustomAccordionComponentTokensProvider())"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It is also possible to use your own semantic tokens providers for this component tokens providers:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["    \/\/ Uses by default here:","    \/\/ - Orange